{{!
    @template tool_certificate/verify_certificate_results

    The result of a certificate code check on admin/tool/certificate/index.php.

    theme_sentientia override, QW-CERT-VERIFY (2026-11-19). tool_certificate
    printed a bare "Not verified" error for a code that matches no issued
    certificate, with nothing to say what that means or what to do next.
    The not-found result now explains it and is announced to screen readers
    (role="alert"). A matching code still renders tool_certificate's own
    result partial (tool_certificate/verify_certificate_result), unchanged.

    Classes required for JS:
    * None

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * None

    Context variables required for this template:
    * success - Whether the code matched an issued certificate
    * message - tool_certificate's "Verified" or "Not verified" text
    * issue - The matched issue, for tool_certificate/verify_certificate_result

    Example context (json):
    {
        "success": false,
        "message": "Not verified"
    }
}}
{{#success}}
    {{#issue}}
        {{> tool_certificate/verify_certificate_result }}
    {{/issue}}
{{/success}}
{{^success}}
<div class="alert alert-danger alert-block sentientia-certverify-notfound" role="alert">
    <p class="font-weight-bold mb-1">{{message}}</p>
    <p class="mb-0">{{#str}}certverify_notfound, theme_sentientia{{/str}}</p>
</div>
{{/success}}
